akaOS has no System V shared memory, so cairo must not build the X11 shared
memory image path.  The XShm protocol headers are present in the graphics
sysroot, which makes the build believe that the shared memory path is
usable.  Dropping the two protocol header checks keeps the shared memory
code out of the library, and the sources that include the System V shared
memory headers unconditionally compile against the empty headers that the
build provides.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -374,10 +374,8 @@
 
   extra_headers = ['X11/Xlibint.h', 'X11/Xproto.h']
   check_headers += [
     ['X11/extensions/XShm.h', {'extra-headers': extra_headers}],
-    ['X11/extensions/shmproto.h', {'extra-headers': extra_headers}],
-    ['X11/extensions/shmstr.h', {'extra-headers': extra_headers}],
   ]
   deps += [x11_dep, xext_dep]
 
